# Notifications: inline reply (the freedesktop `inline-reply` action and
# NotificationReplied signal, which Quickshell implements). The server
# advertises it, and a toast whose sender asked for it gets a Reply button
# that opens a field with Send and Cancel; Send hands the text to the sender
# and dismisses the toast. While a field is open the toast's countdown stops
# and the toast surface takes keyboard focus on demand, so an on-screen
# keyboard can type into it. Stored history rows can't be answered and get
# no button. Messages apps use it to reply to a text without opening the
# app (TELEPHONY-APPS-PLAN §7.2).
#
# Against Omarchy 4.0.6 (edge 4.0.6-1).
# 2026-11-06: notifications rewritten: popups - deck of Toast cards — regenerated against Omarchy 4.5.0-3, same
# semantic change (the previous revision carries the 4.4-era hunks).

# 2026-11-06: notifications plugin rewritten around 4.5 (popups became a key-based deck of Toast.qml cards): reply UI into Toast.qml, helpers/openReplies/sendReply and OnDemand keyboard focus into Service.qml, inlineReplySupported on the server. NotificationCard.qml no longer exists. — regenerated against Omarchy 4.5.0-3, same
# semantic change (the previous revision carries the 4.4-era hunks).

